WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.400
-Welcome back to the show.
Yeah, they love you, buddy.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.601
-Whew!
-We go back a long ways.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:09.601
Do you remember
the first time we hung out?

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:10.868
-The Derby.
-The Kentucky Derby.

00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:12.467
-The Kentucky Derby.
-I was onstage.

00:00:12.467 --> 00:00:15.934
I was dating my now-wife.
And I was dating her.

00:00:15.934 --> 00:00:17.334
And I jumped on the stage

00:00:17.334 --> 00:00:19.167
and I was singing with the band
or something like that.

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:22.000
-You sing? No.
-Yeah, twist my arm.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.534
Yeah, I was doing --
It was yelling, really.

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:26.300
And I got off the stage.
I go, "Where's Nancy?"

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.300
And they go, "Oh,
your girlfriend is so cool, man.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.067
She's over there hanging
with the Manning brothers."

00:00:30.067 --> 00:00:31.601
And she was
chugging a bottle of vodka.

00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:34.167
-Yeah. That's what we do.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:35.601
-I go, "Honey,
you don't do that."

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:36.767
She's like,
"Those guys are just so fun."

00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:38.400
I go, "Oh, my gosh."

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.000
-I didn't see her
the next day at the Derby.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.701
-She didn't make it
to the Derby. No, no.

00:00:41.701 --> 00:00:43.000
We didn't -- No.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.300
Right now, you're the number-1
trending video

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:46.667
on the Internet, by the way.

00:00:46.667 --> 00:00:48.033
Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
-This is really funny.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.801
You did this
with Omaha Productions.

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:55.601
You wore a disguise
and tried out as a walk-on

00:00:55.601 --> 00:00:57.000
for the
Penn State football team.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:59.701
-Yes. Yes. Chad Powers.

00:00:59.701 --> 00:01:01.367
-Chad Powers.
Can I just show everyone?

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:02.601
This is Chad Powers.
-Ooh, yes.

00:01:02.601 --> 00:01:05.467
That's a good-looking man
right there.

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:06.968
-Dude, I want to show
everyone a clip,

00:01:06.968 --> 00:01:07.968
'cause it's really good.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:09.267
Take a look at this.

00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:10.767
-Hey. I'm Chad Powers.

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:13.200
Think fast, run fast.
Think fast, run fast.

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.601
Look up "arm" in the dictionary,
you see a picture of Chad.

00:01:16.601 --> 00:01:18.534
Chad Powers.
You ain't seen nothing like him.

00:01:20.934 --> 00:01:22.334
-Is he good?

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.834
-Chad Powers, you're ineligible.

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:27.067
-I thought I had it, boys.

00:01:27.067 --> 00:01:28.634
But, you know, I'm sorry.

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:31.067
But, you know...

00:01:31.067 --> 00:01:33.667
I'm just a 41-year-old who just
wants to play ball, man.

00:01:33.667 --> 00:01:36.667
I'm just trying to get back out
there, play some ball.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:39.033
-Yeah, I mean, come on.
That was so fun.

00:01:39.033 --> 00:01:41.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:45.234
First of all, how --
how did Chad Powers --

00:01:45.234 --> 00:01:46.934
How did you pull this off?
Who knew?

00:01:46.934 --> 00:01:50.067
-Well, I mean, I think just
a great flow, a mustache,

00:01:50.067 --> 00:01:53.801
and a great name,
a lot of good things happen.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:55.234
-How did you come up
with Chad Powers?

00:01:55.234 --> 00:01:57.667
-Well, he's got two --
really three great uncles.

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:00.234
He's got Austin Powers.

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.267
-What a great backstory.

00:02:01.267 --> 00:02:03.334
-He's got Kenny Powers.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:04.567
And then Uncle Rico.

00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:07.033
So, I mean,
there's a combination there.

00:02:07.033 --> 00:02:08.601
-But did people freak out
and were like,

00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:11.601
"Hey, I'm actually
threatened by Chad Powers."

00:02:11.601 --> 00:02:13.501
-Oh, yeah, no,
I was slingin' it.

00:02:13.501 --> 00:02:14.667
-Yeah, of course you were.
-Chad can throw it.

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:16.601
Chad can really throw it.
He's a good player.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:19.234
He would have made the team,
but he's ineligible.

00:02:19.234 --> 00:02:20.367
-But I was
talking to you backstage.

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:21.901
I go,
"That was cool you do that."

00:02:21.901 --> 00:02:24.100
And I go, "Have you ever been

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:26.501
recognized for
a different celebrity?"

00:02:26.501 --> 00:02:28.467
And you said, "A lot"?
It comes up all the time.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:29.868
-It comes up all the time.

00:02:29.868 --> 00:02:31.801
Just, you know,
not too long ago, this summer,

00:02:31.801 --> 00:02:34.267
I'm taking the girls fishing,
and we're kind of driving.

00:02:34.267 --> 00:02:37.067
And I pull over to get some
water, get some snacks,

00:02:37.067 --> 00:02:38.501
go into a store.

00:02:38.501 --> 00:02:39.901
And, you know,
I get to the counter,

00:02:39.901 --> 00:02:41.801
and the guy
looks at me and goes,

00:02:41.801 --> 00:02:43.601
"Are you who I think you are?"

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.634
I'm like, "Yeah, I think so."

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:48.734
He goes, "Oh, my gosh!
Michael Phelps is any store!"

00:02:50.534 --> 00:02:53.200
He's like, "Everybody, come out!
It's Michael Phelps!"

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.133
I'm like, "Whoa. No, no, no.

00:02:55.133 --> 00:02:57.567
No, no, no.
I'm not Michael Phelps."

00:02:57.567 --> 00:03:00.601
He's like, "So you lied to me?"
I'm like, "No.

00:03:00.601 --> 00:03:02.801
I just thought
who you thought I was

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:05.200
is not who I am
and you thought I was not

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:06.567
who I think I thought
you were or whatever.

00:03:06.567 --> 00:03:09.033
-Now, I can kind of see it.
-Something like that.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:15.534
-Yeah, you can kind of do it.
-That looks like Blue Steel.

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:17.801
-Yeah, he's gonna do a
Blue Steel.

00:03:17.801 --> 00:03:18.801
-Yeah.

00:03:18.801 --> 00:03:19.901
-I want to talk about your show,

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.200
but I also want to
talk about football.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.400
Of course, the big story
everyone's talking about

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.601
is Tom Brady.

00:03:23.601 --> 00:03:26.467
He's back. He retired.
Then he didn't retire.

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:29.133
Did you know that he was --
-I had a feeling.

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:31.400
I saw him not too long
after he retired.

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.167
And -- "Hey, congratulations."

00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:34.734
He was like,
"Well, you never know.

00:03:34.734 --> 00:03:36.167
Like, I'm still working out
a little bit."

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.601
I'm like, "Oh, yeah,
he's coming back."

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:39.734
100%."

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:41.334
-Yeah. But when you retired,
you said --

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.801
-I knew. I was like,
"I am not doing anything.

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:45.701
I'm taking a month,
I'm taking two months off.

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:46.767
I'm not going to train.

00:03:46.767 --> 00:03:48.400
Like, I just --
I want to relax."

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:50.834
And, you know, when I saw,
he was like, "Yeah..."

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:53.667
I mean, I knew 1,000%
I was not playing football.

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:57.467
If there's like
a 10% chance or a 2% chance,

00:03:57.467 --> 00:03:58.567
then you're coming back.

00:03:58.567 --> 00:03:59.934
-Yeah. I know
you're friendly with him,

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:02.968
but do you ever remind Tom
that you're the only quarterback

00:04:02.968 --> 00:04:05.434
in NFL history to beat him
twice in a Super Bowl?

00:04:05.434 --> 00:04:07.868
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I do not, I do not.

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:09.701
-I'm just saying,
it's just something --

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:11.000
something that might come up.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.000
-I see Tom, and we're friendly.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.367
And I never bring it up to him

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:17.167
because, I mean, the guy's got
seven Super Bowl rings.

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:18.300
He's MVP.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:20.901
I have no bragging rights
anywhere near him.

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:24.200
But he --
-He's got three more fingers.

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:28.434
-He will bring up the 2007 game,
when they were undefeated.

00:04:28.434 --> 00:04:31.000
They would have gone down as
the greatest team of all time

00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:34.434
and go undefeated,
and he can't say that now.

00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:35.434
And he blames me.

00:04:35.434 --> 00:04:37.501
And I'm okay with that.

00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:38.968
I can accept that.

00:04:38.968 --> 00:04:40.567
I took one for the team,
you know?

00:04:40.567 --> 00:04:42.634
-Yeah, you really did.
Yeah, exactly. Yeah.

00:04:42.634 --> 00:04:44.834
Yeah, well, every now and then,
if you want to bring it up

00:04:44.834 --> 00:04:46.734
to him, it's always
good to -- humbling --

00:04:46.734 --> 00:04:48.334
just humble him a little bit.

00:04:48.334 --> 00:04:49.434
You're very, very busy.

00:04:49.434 --> 00:04:52.601
You've got
the ManningCast on ESPN

00:04:52.601 --> 00:04:55.234
with your brother, who's --
Gosh, he's so funny, as well.

00:04:55.234 --> 00:04:57.868
You guys together are just --
-He's funny-looking.

00:04:57.868 --> 00:04:59.267
Funny-looking.
-Oh, he's funny-looking.

00:04:59.267 --> 00:05:00.501
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:00.501 --> 00:05:02.667
But you're also
the co-owner of Gotham FC.

00:05:02.667 --> 00:05:03.868
-Yes.

00:05:03.868 --> 00:05:05.534
-This is a professional
women's soccer team.

00:05:05.534 --> 00:05:07.434
-Yes. It's right here
in New Jersey.

00:05:07.434 --> 00:05:08.901
It's the
New York/New Jersey team.

00:05:08.901 --> 00:05:11.200
And it's right in our backyard,
where we live.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:13.367
They practice
15, 20 minutes away.

00:05:13.367 --> 00:05:15.067
They play at Red Bull Arena
in New Jersey.

00:05:15.067 --> 00:05:18.100
And really got involved because
when I grew up,

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:19.534
my dad played
professional football.

00:05:19.534 --> 00:05:21.200
He retired when
I was 3 years old.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.367
But we'd still
go to Saints practices

00:05:23.367 --> 00:05:24.501
and we'd go to games.

00:05:24.501 --> 00:05:26.033
And I got to go in
the locker room and meet

00:05:26.033 --> 00:05:28.300
these players
who were my heroes.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.534
And I really wanted the
same experience for my kids.

00:05:30.534 --> 00:05:32.334
I have four kids,
but I have three girls,

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:33.534
and they're all athletes.

00:05:33.534 --> 00:05:36.133
And for them to see these
professional athletes

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:38.234
and go to practice and meet them
and go to the games

00:05:38.234 --> 00:05:40.067
and say, "Hey, you know --"
I want them to have

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:42.901
role models and to show them
that it's cool to play sports,

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:45.367
and if you work hard, you can be
a professional athlete.

00:05:45.367 --> 00:05:47.067
You don't have to,
but, like, you know,

00:05:47.067 --> 00:05:50.534
just to have someone
to look up to

00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:53.467
and, you know,
give these girls an opportunity.

00:05:53.467 --> 00:05:55.400
I love that they're playing
professional sports.

00:05:55.400 --> 00:05:57.234
And just think, you know,

00:05:57.234 --> 00:05:59.634
sports are so great for
everybody to get involved in.

00:05:59.634 --> 00:06:01.334
-Good for you.
I like that you're doing that.

00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:02.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
I have two girls, too.

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:04.667
They'd love that.

00:06:04.667 --> 00:06:06.467
So, "The Eli Manning Show."

00:06:06.467 --> 00:06:09.467
-Yes.
-It's back for a second season.

00:06:09.467 --> 00:06:11.067
Groundbreaking show.

00:06:11.067 --> 00:06:13.133
-Yes.
-Tell me what happens.

00:06:13.133 --> 00:06:14.534
Describe what happens
on the show.

00:06:14.534 --> 00:06:16.701
-Okay.
So, it's really a new concept.

00:06:16.701 --> 00:06:18.334
I don't think
it's ever been done before.

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:19.868
I'm a host and I have a show.

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:21.067
and I invite guests on,

00:06:21.067 --> 00:06:23.234
and they come
and they sit in a chair.

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:25.067
And I'll ask them questions.

00:06:25.067 --> 00:06:29.000
Sometimes, they're promoting
something -- a show, a movie.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.834
Sometimes,
we do skits and, like,

00:06:30.834 --> 00:06:32.767
different games or sing songs.

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:33.801
-Wow. Wow.

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:35.100
-Have you ever
heard of anything --

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:37.801
-No, I've never heard of
anything like that in my life.

00:06:37.801 --> 00:06:39.834
"The Eli Manning Show."
-It's original.

00:06:39.834 --> 00:06:42.000
-Yeah. The title is good.
-We get a lot of Giants fans.

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:43.167
A lot of Giants fans.
-Exactly.

00:06:43.167 --> 00:06:45.434
-It's got a new title.
-Is it hard for you?

00:06:45.434 --> 00:06:47.033
It is interesting
and it's a different thing

00:06:47.033 --> 00:06:49.000
to be a talk show host
from being a quarterback.

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.767
I mean, obviously.
-Yeah, it is hard.

00:06:51.767 --> 00:06:52.934
I think it's a natural --

00:06:52.934 --> 00:06:54.701
It's a natural just,
you know, progression.

00:06:54.701 --> 00:06:56.234
-Yeah, a normal, natural thing.
-Yeah.

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:57.434
-You're very good at it.
-Yeah.

00:06:57.434 --> 00:06:59.200
-Season 1, you had
some giant names on there.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:01.667
-Yeah.
-And it's Season 2.

00:07:01.667 --> 00:07:03.167
Who do you got
coming up for this season?

00:07:03.167 --> 00:07:05.467
-Well, we had Ryan Reynolds.
-You had Bill Murray.

00:07:05.467 --> 00:07:06.667
-Yeah, we had
Bill Murray last year.

00:07:06.667 --> 00:07:08.234
We have you. You're coming on.
-That's right.

00:07:08.234 --> 00:07:09.701
-Yeah!
-I'm very excited about that.

00:07:09.701 --> 00:07:11.167
-Yes.
-I'm very excited.

00:07:11.167 --> 00:07:12.367
We're going to
play some cornhole.

00:07:12.367 --> 00:07:14.334
-Cornhole, let's go.
-Let's go for it, bud.

00:07:14.334 --> 00:07:16.133
You're going to go down.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:17.767
Here's a peek at
"The Eli Manning Show."

00:07:17.767 --> 00:07:18.901
Take a look at this.

00:07:18.901 --> 00:07:20.133
-Can we get
two regular hot dogs?

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:22.601
-Two regular hot dogs coming up.

00:07:22.601 --> 00:07:23.968
Some onions.
Just some regular onions.

00:07:23.968 --> 00:07:25.567
Look at this.

00:07:25.567 --> 00:07:27.601
Boom, boom, boom.
Wait. I have a question.

00:07:27.601 --> 00:07:28.634
Have you heard that
"The Eli Manning Show"

00:07:28.634 --> 00:07:31.167
is coming back for Season 2?

00:07:31.167 --> 00:07:33.267
-The what?
-"The Eli Manning Show."

00:07:33.267 --> 00:07:35.133
You haven't seen
"The Eli Manning Show?"

00:07:35.133 --> 00:07:36.434
-What is it on?

00:07:36.434 --> 00:07:39.167
-I don't -- Don't ask me the
hard questions like that.

00:07:39.167 --> 00:07:40.934
You know? It's on YouTube.
-We'll look it up.

00:07:41.033 --> 00:07:45.567
-I got pretzels and hot dogs.
Pretzels and hot dogs.

00:07:45.567 --> 00:07:48.133
How you doing, sir? Hot dog?

00:07:48.133 --> 00:07:50.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.801 --> 00:07:53.601
[ Cymbal crash, sad tuba plays ]

00:07:53.601 --> 00:07:55.667
-He still wins!
-That hurt.

00:07:55.667 --> 00:07:58.634
-That hurt you right there.
Eli Manning, everybody.

00:07:58.634 --> 00:08:00.300
Check out
"The Eli Manning Show,"

00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:03.801
streaming now on
the Giants' YouTube channel.

